== S4 the maximal closure K_E = dualW(K_gen) (R5)
PASS A2.10  [identity] R5(a): F lies in K_E (it is A2.4)
PASS A2.11  [witness] R5(b): <psi| pauliW F |psi> < 0, so F is not in Q3: K_E is strictly larger than Q3 -- value -1/8
PASS A2.12  [witness] R5(c): R0 is a rotation and ipW(actT R0 F, cnot(prodState (0,-1,0) (0,1,0))) < 0: actT R0 maps F in K_E out of K_E, so IE1 fails for K_E -- value -2/5
PASS C4  [countercontrol] countercontrol: actT R0 phiW (a member of Q3, inside K_E) is >= 0 on the sampled generators -- minimum 0 over 200 generators
PASS A2.13  [identity] R5(d) membership: phiW lies in K_E: ipW(phiW, prodState x y) = SOS and ipW(phiW, cnot(prodState x y)) = (1 + x1)(1 + y3) >= 0 on the ball
PASS A2.14  [witness] R5(d): famI for the uniform K_E at X = F, Y = phiW, E' = cnot(prodState e2 (-e3)), F' = cnot(prodState e2 e2) is negative -- value -1/2
NOTE [written] A2.W4  -- E' and F' are generators of K_gen; every generator g of K_gen lies in dualW K_E because ipW(g, w) >= 0 for w in K_E = dualW K_gen by definition. So FourCopyCoherent fails for the uniform K_E; K_E contains the products (A2.15), lies in maxCone and is a convex cone, so by Lemma B1 [D] H fails for it.
PASS A2.15  [identity] R5(e): ipW(prodState x y, cnot(prodState u v)) = pairVal(hom x, hom y, cnot(prodState u v)) and ipW(prodState x y, prodState u v) = (1 + x.u)(1 + y.v), symbolic
NOTE [written] A2.W5  -- hom x = 2 ehom(sharp effect (1 + x.z)/2) for |x| <= 1, so pairVal(hom x, hom y, w) = 4 prodEffVal >= 0 for w in maxCone; cnot(prodState u v) is in maxCone by the landed cnot_prodState_mem_maxCone; and (1 + x.u)(1 + y.v) >= 0 on the ball. So every product state lies in K_E.
NOTE [written] A2.W6  -- the interval: every convex cone K that contains the product states, lies in maxCone and is cnot-invariant satisfies K_gen <= K (it contains the products and their cnot images) and K <= K_E (cnot K = K lies in maxCone, so K lies in maxCone /\ cnot(maxCone); dualW(SEP) = maxCone because the homogenized effect vectors of the ball are the cone L of hom-points, landed lor_ehom and isEffectOn_affOf; and dualW(cnot SEP) = cnot(dualW SEP) by A2.1). Q3 and the landed foil K_cl lie in this interval. Both endpoints are closed (K_gen: the convex hull of two compact sets, cone over a compact base; K_E: a dual cone), contain the products, are cnot-invariant, and fail IE1 and FCC (A2.6-A2.9, A2.12-A2.14).

== S5 the identities behind K_gen <= Q3 <= K_E (R6)
PASS A2.16  [identity] R6: pauliW(prodState x y) = rho(x) (x) rho(y), pauliW(cnot w) = CNOT pauliW(w) CNOT^dagger and ipW E X = tr(4 pauliW(E) pauliW(X)), symbolic
NOTE [written] A2.W7  -- with the standard facts (Kronecker products and unitary conjugates of positive semidefinite matrices are positive semidefinite; tr(AB) >= 0 for A, B positive semidefinite) and rho(x) >= 0 for |x| <= 1: every generator of K_gen lies in Q3, so K_gen <= Q3; every member of Q3 pairs nonnegatively with every generator of K_gen, so Q3 <= dualW(K_gen) = K_E. Both inclusions are strict by A2.5 with A2.7 (T_psi in Q3 \ K_gen) and by A2.10 with A2.11 (F in K_E \ Q3).

